==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhakə/|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gml|de}} {{term|hakke|lang=gml}}. Also {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|hakka||animal heel|lang=goh}}, which has no attested continuation in [[w:Middle High German|Middle High German]], however. Compare {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|hak|lang=de}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f||Hacken}}

# {{context|regional|chiefly|northern and central Germany|lang=de}} [[heel]] (of the foot)
# {{context|regional|chiefly|northern and central Germany|lang=de}} the back of the [[shoe]], which is around the [[heel]] (including or excluding the [[sole]], for which alone {{term|Absatz|lang=de}} is used)

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l/de|Ferse}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|hacke|lang=gmh}}. Pertaining to {{term|hacken||to chop|lang=de}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f||Hacken}}

# [[hoe]]

